* mklibs - build the c3 version-2-ABI C libraries on the target (OS-9).
*
* *** UNTESTED on real OS-9 yet - this is the build-on-target starting point;
* *** validate/adjust under emulation.  It mirrors the host makefiles:
* ***   src/lib/sys.a/makefile   -> syslib.l, cstart.r
* ***   src/lib/lib.a/makefile   -> main.l
* ***   src/lib/lib.c/makefile   -> cstuff.l
* *** and the top lib/makefile:   clib.l = cstuff.l + main.l + syslib.l (+ math)
* *** Math (fmath/imath) is NOT built here - add it when the MC6839 FP runtime
* *** is in place; until then programs using the math1 library will not link.
*
* Run it as:   chd /dd/src; mklibs
* Needs in the execution path:  c3 rma  (from /dd/CMDS)  and  merge  (OS-9 system)
* Produces:    /dd/lib/cstart.r  /dd/lib/sys.l  /dd/lib/clib.l
*
* rma assembles a .a source to a .r relocatable; c3 -r compiles a .c to a .r;
* a .l library is just its .r modules concatenated (merge ... >lib.l).

